<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Exchange from '#src/lib/Exchange.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/handlers/post',
        '/handlers/mount-paths',
        '/helpers/validate-json',
        '/reactive/refresh',
        '/handlers/clients',
        '/data/store',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/rpc.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a plain handler is the reactive of itself, and a repeated call joins it — 16.6'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealDetail.test.ts',
            from: ["test('picking a deal loads the one its args name'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/rpc.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a generator handler streams, and the value is its chunks'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/url.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a record or a list of records rides the query as its canonical JSON — 30.28'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/diffOps.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a keyed list is changed row by row, and the ops rebuild it — 18.41'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/durableFollow.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a restart over the same store keeps the version, and the patches since — 18.42, 18.43'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/wireCopy.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a copy given a debounce sends one request for the keys a page reaches inside the window",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/appAddresses.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('rpc.tool is the name MCP lists the handler by, under a mount too",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Read one deal by its id">
        <p>Write the read in a handler file. The parameter's annotation is its <code>Args</code>,
            checked on every call, and <code>description</code> is the sentence every surface
            shows.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { refuse } from '@abide/abide'
            import { GET } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { DEALS } from './lib/DEALS.server.ts'

            export default GET(
                ({ id }: { id: string }) =>
                    DEALS.find((deal) => deal.id === id) ?? refuse(404),
                { description: 'One deal, by id.' },
            )
        `} />
        <p>That file answers at its path. Here is the CRM's, asked over HTTP when this page
            loaded:</p>
        <Exchange path="/deals/getDeal?id=d1" />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Show the deal a page picks">
        <p>Import the handler file and call it inside a <code>reactive.derived</code>. The call answers a
            promise, and the <code>reactive.derived</code> makes it live: the page reads
            <code>deal.name</code> by name and loads again when <code>id</code> changes.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import { reactive } from '@abide/abide'
            import getDeal from './getDeal.handler.ts'

            let id = reactive('d1')
            const deal = reactive.derived(() => getDeal({ id }))
            </script>

            <button onclick={() => (id = 'd2')}>Next deal</button>
            <h2>{deal.name}</h2>
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Send the activity archive an entry at a time">
        <p>Write the handler as an async generator and it streams. A <code>reactive.derived</code>
            reading it holds every entry that has arrived, and its <code>busy()</code> stays true
            until the stream closes.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { GET } from '@abide/abide/server'

            const OLDER = [
                { on: '2026-09-02', note: 'Intro call, asked for pricing' },
                { on: '2026-09-09', note: 'Sent the proposal' },
                { on: '2026-10-01', note: 'Signed for 40 seats' },
            ]

            export default GET(async function* () {
                for (const entry of OLDER) {
                    await Bun.sleep(600) // a slow archive
                    yield entry
                }
            })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Link to the deals export as a download">
        <p>A link cannot call a handler, so give it <code>url()</code>: the address from the
            file's path and the mount. A handler returning a <code>Blob</code> answers with the
            blob's own type.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import exportDeals from './exportDeals.handler.ts'
            </script>

            <a href={exportDeals.url()} download="deals.csv">Download deals</a>
        `} />
        <p>The CRM's export, and the CRM's answer:</p>
        <Exchange path="/deals/exportDeals" />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Filter the deals by a record">
        <p>Give an arg a record, or a list of records, and it rides the URL as JSON with its keys
            sorted, so one filter is one address. A list of plain values repeats its name. The
            handler reads both back as its <code>Args</code> declares them.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="browser" code={`
            import searchDeals from './searchDeals.handler.ts'

            const address = searchDeals.url({
                filter: { stage: 'won', owner: 'ada' },
                ids: [1, 2],
            })
            decodeURIComponent(address)
            // /deals/searchDeals?filter={"owner":"ada","stage":"won"}&ids=1&ids=2
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Spot the assistant drafting a report as it streams">
        <p><code>tool</code> is the name MCP lists the handler by, the name a model's
            <code>tool_use</code> carries. It is read off the route, so it stays the same under a
            sub-path.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="browser" code={`
            import draftReport from './draftReport.handler.ts'

            // 'post_ops_draftReport'
            const drafting = (block: { type: string; name?: string }) =>
                block.type === 'tool_use' && block.name === draftReport.tool
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Reload only the pipeline stages a win changed">
        <p>Pass the handler's <code>refresh</code> a pattern of its args, and the entries matching
            it load again while every other stage stays as it is.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="browser" code={`
            import getStage from './getStage.handler.ts'
            import winDeal from './winDeal.handler.ts'

            await winDeal()
            getStage.refresh({ stage: 'lead' })
            getStage.refresh({ stage: 'won' })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Send every tab the call just logged, and nothing else">
        <p>Make the read <code>global</code> and write it on the server with
            <code>patch</code>. Every page reading it follows it, and a change reaches each one as
            the JSON Patch from the value it replaced, so a logged call is one row on the wire
            rather than the list again. <code>key</code> says which row is which.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { POST } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import listCalls, { type Call } from './listCalls.handler.ts'

            export default POST(({ id, note }: Call) => {
                listCalls.patch((held) => {
                    if (!held.some((call) => call.id === id)) held.push({ id, note })
                })
            })
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Search the deals once the typing stops">
        <p>Give the read a <code>debounce</code>, and every page calling it is held to it: the first
            query is searched at once, and one typed after it once the typing pauses rather than
            once per keystroke. The page reads the handler as it would any other.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { GET } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { DEALS } from './lib/DEALS.server.ts'

            export default GET(
                ({ q }: { q: string }) => {
                    const names: string[] = []
                    for (const deal of DEALS)
                        if (deal.name.toLowerCase().includes(q.toLowerCase()))
                            names.push(deal.name)
                    return names
                },
                { debounce: 300 },
            )
        `} />
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import { reactive } from '@abide/abide'
            import searchDeals from '../searchDeals.handler.ts'

            let q = reactive('')
            const found = reactive.derived(() => searchDeals({ q }))
            </script>

            <input bind:value={q}>
            {#for name of found}<p>{name}</p>{/for}
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Keep the call log's versions across a restart">
        <p>Give the read a <code>store</code> that keeps a log, <code>store.sqlite</code> or
            <code>store.redis</code>, and each change is a numbered record in it. A restarted
            server stands at the same version, so a page that reconnects is sent only the patches
            it missed. A second server on the same store applies the first one's records and sends
            them to its own followers.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { GET, store } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { crmDatabase } from '../pipeline/lib/crmDatabase.server.ts'

            export type Call = { id: string; note: string }

            export default GET((): Call[] => [], {
                global: true,
                key: 'id',
                store: store.sqlite<Call[]>(crmDatabase, 'calls'),
            })
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
